 the right flip for your needs.\"}]]}]\nd:[\"$\",\"details\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"card\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"style\":{\"fontSize\":\"1.05rem\",\"fontWeight\":\"600\",\"cursor\":\"pointer\",\"padding\":\"0.5rem 0\",\"listStyle\":\"none\",\"display\":\"flex\",\"justifyContent\":\"space-between\",\"alignItems\":\"center\"},\"children\":[\"Can I undo a flip?\",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"style\":{\"fontSize\":\"1.25rem\",\"color\":\"var(--success)\"},\"children\":\"+\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted\",\"style\":{\"fontSize\":\"0.9rem\",\"margin\":\"0.5rem 0 0 0\",\"paddingTop\":\"0.5rem\",\"borderTop\":\"1px solid var(--border-color)\"},\"children\":\"Yes, undoing a flip is simple. If you apply a horizontal or vertical flip and want to revert, just click the corresponding flip button a second time. This restores the pixel coordinates to their original layout, allowing you to preview different configurations without any risk. You can experiment freely since nothing is permanent until you download.\"}]]}]\ne:[\"$\",\"details\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"card\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"style\":{\"fontSize\":\"1.05rem\",\"fontWeight\":\"600\",\"cursor\":\"pointer\",\"padding\":\"0.5rem 0\",\"listStyle\":\"none\",\"display\":\"flex\",\"justifyContent\":\"space-between\",\"alignItems\":\"center\"},\"children\":[\"Does flipping affect image quality?\",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"style\":{\"fontSize\":\"1.25rem\",\"color\":\"var(--success)\"},\"children\":\"+\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted\",\"style\":{\"fontSize\":\"0.9rem\",\"margin\":\"0.5rem 0 0 0\",\"paddingTop\":\"0.5rem\",\"borderTop\":\"1px solid var(--border-color)\"},\"children\":\"No, flipping your images does not reduce quality. The mirroring calculations are processed losslessly using the HTML5 Canvas API in your browser. The pixels are flipped mathematically across the axis, preserving the origina